AI for Industry Challenge: Vision-Guided Cable Insertion
Participant solution by pranay172 (https://github.com/pranay172)

This repository is the AI for Industry Challenge toolkit,
https://github.com/intrinsic-dev/aic, with its history up to commit
ced3678cadaa446911a7d14c11b6fd1399509f08 (2026-05-11), the last toolkit
commit before the qualification deadline, plus one commit containing this
solution. The toolkit is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). Files under aic_utils/aic_isaac carry their own
BSD-3-Clause license.

Added by this work: the participant policy and perception modules in
aic_model/aic_model/ (every file except the toolkit's __init__.py,
aic_model.py and policy.py), aic_model/models/, aic_model/tools/,
benchmarks/, scripts/, tests/, pytest.ini, docs/solution/, docs/assets/
(except task_board.jpg), .github/workflows/tests.yml and this NOTICE.

docs/assets/task_board.jpg is a downscaled copy of aic_task_board.png from
the toolkit repository's media branch (commit 8012d52), by the challenge
organizers.

policy.py, ground_truth.py and the policy_* modules split from them began as
the toolkit's aic_model/aic_model/policy.py, so they keep its Intrinsic
copyright header as the Apache License requires; their content beyond that is
this work.

Toolkit files modified by this work:
- aic_model/aic_model/policy.py: replaced by the participant policy entry point.
- aic_model/aic_model/aic_model.py: reworked goal execution. One goal at a
  time, a policy worker that stops cooperatively on cancel, deactivate or
  shutdown, a hold command when a run is stopped, rejection of motion
  commands from a stopped run, a capture-episode reset at each insert_cable
  call, and tolerance of the signal-shutdown race in the executor.
- aic_example_policies/aic_example_policies/ros/CheatCode.py: sends its pose
  targets through the shared aic_model motion helpers.
- docker/aic_model/Dockerfile: runs aic_model.policy, ships the four
  participant checkpoints with their AIC_* paths, and overlays the policy
  source after the dependency layer.
- docker/docker-compose.yaml: the same checkpoint paths and the solution
  image tag.
- pixi.toml: linux-64 only; pinned build variants (GCC 15.2, Python 3.12,
  NumPy 2.2); PyTorch and torchvision from the CUDA 12.8 index.
- The package pixi.toml files under aic_model, aic_interfaces, aic_utils and
  aic_example_policies: EmPy 3.3.4 and ros2-distro-mutex pins, and runtime
  Python files as aic_model build inputs.
- pixi.lock: re-solved for these manifests.
- .gitignore: ignores local run, capture and test directories.
- README.md: rewritten for this solution.

Removed from the toolkit tree: the toolkit's CI workflows and issue templates
under .github/, which target the upstream repository. This repository's own
workflow, .github/workflows/tests.yml, runs the offline test suite.
